    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="58">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 58</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="58" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa ciningces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_58.lnote.oe.2"/> borh abrece, gebete þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> mid V<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_58.lnote.oe.3"/> pundan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="58" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>Be borhbryce. Gyf hwa kynincges borh abrece, gebete þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> mid V pundum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="58" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa cyninges borh abrece, gebe[te<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_58.lnote.oe.1-2"/>] þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> mid fif pundu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="58" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="351" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis plegium (pacem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_58.lnote.oe.1"/>) regis frangat, emendet V libras.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="58" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="351" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis plegium regis fregerit, emendet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_58.lnote.oe.2-2"/> quinque libris.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="58" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="351" ed="#liebermann"/>[58] Si quis regis fideiussionem soluerit, emendet hoc V libris;</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="58" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="204" ed="#robertson"/>Be borhbryce. Gif hwa kynincges borh abrece, gebete þæt mid V pundum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="284" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif hwa ciningces borh abrece, gebete þæt mid V pundan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>(Vom Bruch der Schutzgewähr. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_58.lnote.de.1"/> einer des Königs Schutzgewähr verletzt, büsse er das mit 5 Pfund [dem Könige].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of the breach of protection. B) If anyone violates the king's protection, let him atone for it with 5 pounds [to the king].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_58.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="205" ed="#robertson"/>Concerning the violation of protection. If anyone violates the king's protection, he shall pay £5 as compensation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_58.whinote.n.4"/><pb n="470" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone violates the king’s surety, he is to compensate for it with five pounds.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="285" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If anyone violates the king’s protection, he shall be penalized five pounds.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="350"><ref target="clause:Af_3">Af 3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. Af. 3</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Grith_11">Grið 11</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="353"><label>paraphrases</label> <ref target="clause:Af_3">Af 3</ref> <quote>When Alfred's domboc was quoted ... Alfred's law was not so much quoted as paraphrased (n. 421: II Cn 58 – 58:2, Af 3)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="353"><label>equivalent</label> <ref target="clause:Grith_11">Grið 11</ref> <quote>As regards II Cn 58 – 58:2 above, note that the form of the equivalent law in Grið 11 is in some ways closer to Alfred's original</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_3">Af 3</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 58-58:2: Grið 11  Af 3</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Grith_11">Grið 11</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 58-58:2: Grið 11  Af 3</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="404"><label>based on</label> <ref target="clause:Af_15">Af 15–17</ref> <quote>II Cn 58 – 59, which were themselves based on nearly related Alfred matter</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="404"><label>based on</label> <ref target="clause:Af_38">Af 38–39.2</ref> <quote>II Cn 58 – 59, which were themselves based on nearly related Alfred matter</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="470"><label>from</label> <ref target="clause:Af_3">Af 3</ref> <quote>from Alfred 3</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">A reads ‘gebe’; Liebermann supplies [te]. Liebermann compares Af 3.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 351, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Be borhbryce</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_58.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr. Dm;</hi> id est p. <hi rend="italic">T; fehlt übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above Dm; id est p. T; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_58.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyninges <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyninges Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_58.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fif pundum <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fif pundum Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_58.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gebe <hi rend="italic">A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gebe A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_58.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">regi <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cb adds regi</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_58.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Neben Af wird 58 bis 58, 2 benutzt durch Grið 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Besides Af, 58 to 58, 2 is used by Grið 11</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_58.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With this clause and the two following, cf. Af. 3; <hi rend="italic">Be Griðe</hi>, 11.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_58.whinote.n.4" n="4" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">470</biblScope></bibl><label>58</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">from Alfred 3</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
